Input: {"question": "What is the population of Elkins?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 0, "end": 55, "text": "Census Bureau, the city has a total area of , all land."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 56, "end": 161, "text": "As of the census of 2000, there were 1,251 people, 485 households, and 370 families residing in the city."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 162, "end": 230, "text": "The population density was 479.7 people per square mile (185.1/km²)."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 231, "end": 308, "text": "There were 518 housing units at an average density of 198.6/sq mi (76.6/km²)."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 309, "end": 507, "text": "The racial makeup of the city was 96.56% White, 0.16% Black or African American, 1.76% Native American, 0.24% Asian, 0.08% Pacific Islander, 0.16% from other races, and 1.04% from two or more races."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 508, "end": 568, "text": "1.20% of the population were Hispanic or Latino of any race."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d00", "start": 569, "end": 579, "text": "There were"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d01", "start": 0, "end": 135, "text": "picturesque, Davis and Elkins each built permanent places of residence, known as Graceland (1893) and Halliehurst (1890), respectively."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d01", "start": 136, "end": 431, "text": "Today, Elkins has an active economic development authority, chamber of commerce, downtown business organization and numerous social, fraternal and service organizations that sponsor annual events like the Mountain State Forest Festival, which brings thousands of people into the city every year."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d01", "start": 432, "end": 541, "text": "As of the census of 2010, there were 7,094 people, 3,038 households, and 1,756 families residing in the city."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d01", "start": 542, "end": 570, "text": "The population density was ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d01", "start": 571, "end": 628, "text": "There were 3,421 housing units at an average density of ."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d01", "start": 629, "end": 658, "text": "The racial makeup of the city"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d02", "start": 0, "end": 65, "text": "no spouse present.The average household and family size was 3.6 ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d02", "start": 66, "end": 109, "text": "The median age in the city was 38.1 years ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d02", "start": 110, "end": 233, "text": "2010 census As of the census of 2010 , there were 7,094 people , 3,038 households , and 1,756 families living in the city ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d02", "start": 234, "end": 313, "text": "The population density was 2,068.2 inhabitants per square mile ( 798.5/km 2 ) ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d02", "start": 314, "end": 408, "text": "There were 3,421 housing units at an average density of 997.4 per square mile ( 385.1/km 2 ) ."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0327-13e42a6f279b:d02", "start": 409, "end": 506, "text": "The racial makeup of the city was 96.5 % White , 1.2 % African American , 0.2 % Native American ,"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-